  "final": "Done. The requested change is implemented and verified.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`src/repository.py`**\n- `find(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` now selects `WHERE id=? AND tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`; a missing, cross-tenant, cross-owner, or soft-deleted row all produce `None`.\n- `listing(connection, tenant, owner)` now selects `WHERE tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY id`.\n- Both queries use only bound `?` parameters, including tenant/owner values that contain quotes.\n- Results still select and decode only `id`, `title`, `body` — no deletion metadata.\n\n**`src/service.py`**\n- `get_document` forwards `(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` to `find`.\n- `list_documents` forwards `(connection, tenant, owner)` to `listing`.\n\n**`checks/security.py`** (new)\n- Covers allowed reads, cross-tenant/cross-owner/deleted IDs returning `None`, list filtering and ordering, empty scopes, exact result field set, and tenant/owner names containing single quotes.\n\n## Verification\n- `python3 checks/public.py` — passed (all assertions).\n- `python3 checks/security.py` — passed.\n- Additional ad-hoc check confirmed ordering with out-of-order insertions, deleted exclusion, and injection-style inputs (`\"1 OR 1=1\"`, `\"t' OR '1'='1\"`) treated as literal data, returning `None`/`[]`.",
